1
00:00:01,940 --> 00:00:02,770
Yeah, yeah!

2
00:00:02,853 --> 00:00:03,683
That's good!

3
00:00:03,766 --> 00:00:04,596
Right where I want it!

4
00:00:19,800 --> 00:00:20,918
Good work, Meester.

5
00:00:21,180 --> 00:00:24,577
As long as we keep moving upwards, we
should ward off any further attacks!

6
00:00:24,660 --> 00:00:25,490
Hmph.

7
00:00:29,020 --> 00:00:30,200
Very interesting.

8
00:00:30,720 --> 00:00:33,497
I think I finally understand
how those backstabbing

9
00:00:33,580 --> 00:00:36,286
hooligans managed to
betray the boss and live.

10
00:00:37,000 --> 00:00:39,520
Seko, did you capture their agonized mugs?

11
00:00:39,780 --> 00:00:42,037
You know how much I love
the totally desperate

12
00:00:42,120 --> 00:00:44,377
contortions they make while
fighting for their lives.

13
00:00:44,460 --> 00:00:45,290
Oh, oh!

14
00:00:47,060 --> 00:00:47,890
Yoooo!

15
00:00:59,180 --> 00:01:01,020
But a vis-simile seko!

16
00:01:01,900 --> 00:01:02,730
Hm.

17
00:01:03,080 --> 00:01:08,480
As our curiosity continues to grow, so
too does the boldness of our keen spirits.

18
00:01:08,800 --> 00:01:13,220
And it is the very same inquisitiveness
that fuels our cognitive evolution.

19
00:01:13,660 --> 00:01:15,580
I yearn to see it.

20
00:01:16,120 --> 00:01:20,897
What glorious grimaces will they unveil as
they wrestle with the cold jaws of death?

21
00:01:20,980 --> 00:01:21,810
Ahh!

22
00:01:22,080 --> 00:01:22,910
Ahh!

23
00:01:23,280 --> 00:01:24,110
Hmm.

24
00:01:24,820 --> 00:01:26,800
That's right, I almost forgot.

25
00:01:27,200 --> 00:01:30,260
A little reward for my intrepid cameraman.

26
00:01:30,820 --> 00:01:32,200
How does two sound? Oh!

27
00:01:33,500 --> 00:01:34,700
You want three?

28
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,706
Gracious, three whole treats?

29
00:01:37,640 --> 00:01:38,470
Ah!

30
00:01:38,553 --> 00:01:39,383
Ah!

31
00:01:39,466 --> 00:01:40,296
Ah!

32
00:01:40,379 --> 00:01:41,209
Greedy mutt.

33
00:01:41,292 --> 00:01:42,122
All right, three it is.

34
00:01:42,205 --> 00:01:43,035
Are you ready, boy?

35
00:01:43,118 --> 00:01:44,557
Because they're coming at you now!

36
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:45,470
Yuck!

37
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:50,120
Oh, whoops, my bad!

38
00:02:04,380 --> 00:02:06,440
psycho, yes, you are! Now go!

39
00:02:07,780 --> 00:02:11,137
I'm counting on you to find
Bucerati and his band of idiots.

40
00:02:11,220 --> 00:02:14,338
Be sure to let them have a
little taste of sanctuary.

41
00:02:24,840 --> 00:02:27,777
I love you,

42
00:02:27,860 --> 00:02:33,117
I love

43
00:02:33,200 --> 00:02:35,080
you

44
00:02:44,320 --> 00:02:45,780
Thank you.

45
00:03:05,080 --> 00:03:07,040
Stay cold

46
00:03:36,172 --> 00:03:37,002
Achimari no Kogelin

47
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,130
Right now,

48
00:04:05,213 --> 00:04:09,157
our number one priority should be making
it to Rome as quickly as possible.

49
00:04:09,240 --> 00:04:11,769
Hey, Giorno, how goes
Narancia's treatment?

50
00:04:12,080 --> 00:04:14,057
Healing him here is going
to be kind of tricky.

51
00:04:14,140 --> 00:04:17,258
His injuries are all teeming
with an aggressive mold.

52
00:04:19,360 --> 00:04:20,360
All right, Mista.

53
00:04:20,620 --> 00:04:21,914
We're clear to ascend.

54
00:04:22,240 --> 00:04:26,475
Let's get to the top of those stairs
and hit the road as fast as we can.

55
00:04:27,760 --> 00:04:28,720
That was cold.

56
00:04:28,960 --> 00:04:30,337
What has gotten into him?

57
00:04:30,420 --> 00:04:31,250
Such a jerk.

58
00:04:31,860 --> 00:04:34,742
He didn't even think to
ask if Narancia was okay.

59
00:04:36,860 --> 00:04:38,500
Also, before that,

60
00:04:39,060 --> 00:04:42,037
when you guys were desperately
struggling to get out of the boat,

61
00:04:42,120 --> 00:04:43,217
remember what he said?

62
00:04:43,300 --> 00:04:48,137
He ordered you to toss the turtle like you
were all just disposable pieces of trash.

63
00:04:48,220 --> 00:04:49,926
What are you so pissed about?

64
00:04:50,060 --> 00:04:51,397
Of course he said that.

65
00:04:51,480 --> 00:04:53,217
I'm the idiot who got on the boat.

66
00:04:53,300 --> 00:04:55,257
I mean, I'm glad we're alive and all,

67
00:04:55,340 --> 00:04:58,987
but don't forget that we nearly
died because of my stupid ass.

68
00:04:59,320 --> 00:05:00,150
Besides,

69
00:05:00,233 --> 00:05:01,997
if Bucciarati hadn't told
me to throw the turtle,

70
00:05:02,080 --> 00:05:04,657
I might have ended up
dropping it in the ocean.

71
00:05:04,740 --> 00:05:06,417
Look, I don't need a lecture.

72
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:11,147
The only thing I'm trying to say is, he
could stand to be a little nicer to us.

73
00:05:12,500 --> 00:05:17,157
I'll admit, I've never really been that
good at talking about feelings and stuff.

74
00:05:17,240 --> 00:05:21,037
But I'm guessing you wouldn't be so
mad if he just asked if you were okay.

75
00:05:21,120 --> 00:05:22,179
Do I got it right?

76
00:05:25,040 --> 00:05:28,157
Difference between you and me is I
already know how Bucciarati thinks.

77
00:05:28,240 --> 00:05:30,657
but it looks like you're
still trying to figure

78
00:05:30,740 --> 00:05:33,117
out how to get inside
that weird head of his.

79
00:05:33,200 --> 00:05:34,030
Excuse me?

80
00:05:34,120 --> 00:05:35,657
What are you trying to say?

81
00:05:35,740 --> 00:05:39,564
Look, all that matters right now
is getting to Rome in one piece.

82
00:05:39,720 --> 00:05:43,317
You'll have all the time you need
to sort out your feelings later.

83
00:05:43,400 --> 00:05:45,420
I'm not feeling too hot right now.

84
00:05:45,980 --> 00:05:47,451
Let me get some shut-eye.

85
00:05:57,700 --> 00:05:59,560
I know we gotta keep climbing,

86
00:05:59,800 --> 00:06:03,447
but what are we gonna do on the
off chance we have to descend?

87
00:06:04,380 --> 00:06:05,210
It's fine.

88
00:06:05,293 --> 00:06:09,964
This village was built into the mountainside,
meaning the roads are on an incline.

89
00:06:10,300 --> 00:06:13,397
Also, keep in mind there's still
some traffic on the outskirts.

90
00:06:13,480 --> 00:06:15,857
The mold has yet to
spread too far from here.

91
00:06:15,940 --> 00:06:19,705
If we can get to a vehicle and
leave immediately, we'll be fine.

92
00:06:19,820 --> 00:06:21,680
We must stay focused on Rome.

93
00:06:22,200 --> 00:06:23,906
So, which car should we take?

94
00:06:24,020 --> 00:06:25,785
The one next to the dead body.

95
00:06:26,340 --> 00:06:30,811
With any luck, we just might be able
to find the key to the ignition on him.

96
00:06:34,740 --> 00:06:37,137
Startled by a mere hand
decaying from the mold.

97
00:06:37,220 --> 00:06:41,457
I'll keep a watch on our rear, while you
sprint to the car as quickly as you can.

98
00:06:41,540 --> 00:06:42,370
Right.

99
00:06:53,060 --> 00:06:55,460
Mister, hold on. Just now.

100
00:06:55,800 --> 00:06:59,180
I felt something. Get a move on. Got it!

101
00:07:06,320 --> 00:07:07,917
Don't just stand there and gawk!

102
00:07:08,000 --> 00:07:09,817
Hurry and climb those stairs like I said!

103
00:07:09,900 --> 00:07:12,194
That's what I'm trying to do, Buterati!

104
00:07:12,780 --> 00:07:13,610
Oh, shit!

105
00:07:13,693 --> 00:07:15,013
We're starting to sink!

106
00:07:15,940 --> 00:07:17,646
It's sliding off of the wall!

107
00:07:19,380 --> 00:07:20,210
What the?

108
00:07:20,293 --> 00:07:24,142
At this rate, the ground's gonna
smalow this whole damn staircase.

109
00:07:24,300 --> 00:07:26,597
This has to be the work of another stand.

110
00:07:26,680 --> 00:07:28,268
Our mold user has a friend.

111
00:07:28,480 --> 00:07:29,600
Screw me sideways.

112
00:07:29,880 --> 00:07:33,497
If we keep sinking, this mold's gonna
melt our asses down into puddles of crap.

113
00:07:33,580 --> 00:07:35,051
We're gonna have to jump.

114
00:07:37,020 --> 00:07:38,640
Hey, my gun!

115
00:07:40,780 --> 00:07:41,900
It's not sinking.

116
00:07:42,660 --> 00:07:46,425
The entire staircase itself is
dissolving right into the ground!

117
00:07:48,880 --> 00:07:49,860
What the hell?

118
00:07:51,460 --> 00:07:52,290
It's them!

119
00:07:52,373 --> 00:07:55,477
They're rushing toward a
location from beneath the ground!

120
00:07:55,560 --> 00:07:57,148
Mista, get on the wall now!

121
00:08:00,520 --> 00:08:01,580
Go, Zipperman!

122
00:08:04,920 --> 00:08:07,560
To counter me this fast, not bad.

123
00:08:07,880 --> 00:08:09,397
But there's something else to their power.

124
00:08:09,480 --> 00:08:13,245
The ground feels oddly hard to
the touch, even through my stand.

125
00:08:13,700 --> 00:08:17,580
Yet I continue to sink in spite
of its solidity. Meanwhile,

126
00:08:17,740 --> 00:08:21,997
my opponent can freely move around
beneath me as if the stairs were liquid.

127
00:08:22,080 --> 00:08:22,910
Merda!

128
00:08:22,993 --> 00:08:24,317
I've no way of finding them!

129
00:08:24,400 --> 00:08:26,000
It's a total guessing game!

130
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:28,297
Get the crap out of your
damn ears, six bullets!

131
00:08:28,380 --> 00:08:29,439
Come back to Papa!

132
00:08:30,760 --> 00:08:31,800
Yee-haw!

133
00:08:38,780 --> 00:08:42,280
A flesh-eating fungus, and
now a subterranean predator.

134
00:08:43,020 --> 00:08:46,726
Both of them deftly working
together in tandem to take us down.

135
00:08:46,920 --> 00:08:48,420
I'll admit I'm impressed.

136
00:08:48,620 --> 00:08:49,660
A flawless duo.

137
00:08:49,920 --> 00:08:52,517
We've yet to encounter
such a pair of killers.

138
00:08:52,600 --> 00:08:57,424
Well, maybe these violent little assholes
should hurry up and get married already.

139
00:09:01,060 --> 00:09:02,707
You were right on the money.

140
00:09:02,840 --> 00:09:06,428
Our decaying friend over there
still got the key to his ride.

141
00:09:11,860 --> 00:09:12,690
Strunzo!

142
00:09:13,420 --> 00:09:15,660
I swear I saw him pop out just now.

143
00:09:15,900 --> 00:09:19,253
The goddamn coward just dove
from the stairs to the wall.

144
00:09:19,680 --> 00:09:21,080
Damn, what now?

145
00:09:22,200 --> 00:09:23,540
Run away, quickly!

146
00:09:26,880 --> 00:09:28,017
God damn it!

147
00:09:28,100 --> 00:09:30,237
Even if we make it to
the car in one piece,

148
00:09:30,320 --> 00:09:32,417
we won't have enough
time to start the engine!

149
00:09:32,500 --> 00:09:34,457
I'll stop this guy dead in his tracks!

150
00:09:34,540 --> 00:09:35,481
You go on ahead!

151
00:09:35,760 --> 00:09:36,797
Don't stop running!

152
00:09:36,880 --> 00:09:38,877
The ground is still in its solid state!

153
00:09:38,960 --> 00:09:40,548
Your bullets will ricochet!

154
00:09:41,760 --> 00:09:44,997
If this quicksand shit's gonna
stay hard like normal ground,

155
00:09:45,080 --> 00:09:47,937
I'll just have to get him when
he tries to pull me under.

156
00:09:48,020 --> 00:09:50,197
This guy likes to hit hard from up close.

157
00:09:50,280 --> 00:09:51,574
I bet his range sucks.

158
00:09:51,840 --> 00:09:55,252
I should be able to see him
the second he tries to get me.

159
00:09:55,340 --> 00:09:57,000
Then it's murder time, baby!

160
00:09:58,740 --> 00:09:59,570
There!

161
00:09:59,653 --> 00:10:01,305
I knew you couldn't stay away!

162
00:10:01,440 --> 00:10:02,800
Now, eat this!

163
00:10:07,340 --> 00:10:08,460
No, mister!

164
00:10:08,900 --> 00:10:10,040
Of freakin' course.

165
00:10:10,280 --> 00:10:12,697
I should've guessed a close
range power base stand

166
00:10:12,780 --> 00:10:15,898
would have some way to defend
itself against bullets.

167
00:10:16,920 --> 00:10:19,817
Although, you're not the only
one who knows that trick.

168
00:10:19,900 --> 00:10:22,197
My little buddies can deflect bullets too!

169
00:10:22,280 --> 00:10:24,221
Those first three shots should...

170
00:10:24,800 --> 00:10:26,120
Oh, come on!

171
00:10:27,680 --> 00:10:30,117
What is he saving me
for later he must think

172
00:10:30,200 --> 00:10:33,024
i've become an easy target
now that i'm wounded?

173
00:10:33,300 --> 00:10:36,535
Hurry and pick up the key
Buchananthi start the engine!

174
00:10:38,500 --> 00:10:41,597
What the hell man get inside the damn car

175
00:10:41,680 --> 00:10:44,797
if we're able to drive
out of this village!

176
00:10:44,880 --> 00:10:48,940
We'll be fine just as long as
we all keep heading to Rome.

177
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:54,437
Where is that guy running off to now?

178
00:10:54,520 --> 00:10:55,350
Ow!

179
00:10:56,760 --> 00:10:57,820
Wait, what?

180
00:10:58,800 --> 00:11:02,057
So, you're tracking our movements
from beneath the earth, huh?

181
00:11:02,140 --> 00:11:03,700
Quite a terrifying power.

182
00:11:04,100 --> 00:11:05,900
But, what is your extent?

183
00:11:06,200 --> 00:11:08,671
Can you really discern my true intentions?

184
00:11:10,300 --> 00:11:12,920
It seems not even you
possess that ability.

185
00:11:13,260 --> 00:11:14,789
I can see it on your face.

186
00:11:25,420 --> 00:11:28,240
THE FACE COUNCIL

187
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:34,580
Arab Nelchi!

188
00:11:46,240 --> 00:11:47,640
My...

189
00:11:52,060 --> 00:11:54,000
My face!

190
00:11:55,120 --> 00:11:56,320
My face!

191
00:12:11,340 --> 00:12:12,170
Huh?

192
00:12:12,253 --> 00:12:13,083
What is it?

193
00:12:14,540 --> 00:12:15,880
Hey, Cioccolata!

194
00:12:17,280 --> 00:12:20,280
Three days ago, you heard the news, right?

195
00:12:20,620 --> 00:12:25,100
You know the stand that the boss put
on the airplane thingy? Yeah, yeah!

196
00:12:25,400 --> 00:12:27,737
Notorious Chase is what I
think I heard it was called!

197
00:12:27,820 --> 00:12:32,157
Now Seko, aren't you supposed to be busy
hunting down those bastards like I asked?

198
00:12:32,240 --> 00:12:33,769
Don't waste time chatting.

199
00:12:34,240 --> 00:12:35,400
Cioccolata, please!

200
00:12:36,160 --> 00:12:39,340
This is important, very important!

201
00:12:41,060 --> 00:12:42,180
Notorious Chase!

202
00:12:43,420 --> 00:12:47,920
Is it a living stand, or
is it a dead stand? Hmm?

203
00:12:48,340 --> 00:12:50,357
Why are you asking all of a sudden?

204
00:12:50,440 --> 00:12:52,793
I know it sounds like a stupid question,

205
00:12:53,360 --> 00:12:54,600
Please answer me!

206
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:58,317
Let's say that Notorious Chase
were here right now with us.

207
00:12:58,400 --> 00:13:01,217
You think your mold would be
able to grow on him at all?

208
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:04,937
Like, do you know if it would
be able to grow on a dead stand?

209
00:13:05,020 --> 00:13:06,255
Notorious Chase, huh?

210
00:13:06,540 --> 00:13:10,357
Isn't that the one whose user was filled
with so much vengeance and hatred,

211
00:13:10,440 --> 00:13:13,797
his stand found a way to live
on even after he was killed?

212
00:13:13,880 --> 00:13:14,720
Who knows?

213
00:13:15,080 --> 00:13:18,897
I confess I'm kind of curious myself,
but I don't have the foggiest idea.

214
00:13:18,980 --> 00:13:21,997
What I do know is that
green tea will putrefy

215
00:13:22,080 --> 00:13:24,845
any living organism it
comes into contact with.

216
00:13:24,960 --> 00:13:29,197
So the mold won't grow on rocks and
other non-alive stuff, is that right?

217
00:13:29,280 --> 00:13:30,240
Forget this!

218
00:13:30,440 --> 00:13:32,857
I asked you to film those
fools with their death row,

219
00:13:32,940 --> 00:13:34,597
so stop dawdling and hop to it!

220
00:13:34,680 --> 00:13:37,100
Yeah, but that's the thing, Cioccolata!

221
00:13:37,360 --> 00:13:41,760
Take a gander at the hill!
Up there! On the road! Huh?

222
00:13:44,500 --> 00:13:47,880
Hey Seko, why am I watching
a car leave the village?

223
00:13:48,280 --> 00:13:51,577
Oh, don't tell me the passengers
are who I think they are!

224
00:13:51,660 --> 00:13:53,660
Why are you letting them get away?

225
00:13:53,840 --> 00:13:55,880
I don't know! I don't know!

226
00:13:56,340 --> 00:13:57,980
It all happened so fast!

227
00:13:58,200 --> 00:14:00,380
He actually hit me right in my face!

228
00:14:00,740 --> 00:14:02,500
That Burjarati guy!

229
00:14:02,920 --> 00:14:06,320
There wasn't any mold
on him, not even a bit!

230
00:14:06,540 --> 00:14:08,797
And I even watched him jump down!

231
00:14:08,880 --> 00:14:12,351
HE SHOULDN'T HAVE BEEN ABLE TO
ATTACK ME FROM WHERE HE WAS!

232
00:14:13,140 --> 00:14:13,970
AAAAAAAH!

233
00:14:14,053 --> 00:14:16,369
THERE'S NO WAY IT COULD
HAVE BEEN POSSIBLE!

234
00:14:17,160 --> 00:14:20,300
HIS BODY MUST SOMEHOW
BE RESISTED TO THE MOLD!

235
00:14:20,520 --> 00:14:22,317
HOW IS THIS EVEN HAPPENING?!

236
00:14:22,400 --> 00:14:24,560
I HAVEN'T THE SLIGHTEST.

237
00:14:26,880 --> 00:14:27,837
You, uh...

238
00:14:27,920 --> 00:14:29,857
you had me fooled for a sec there.

239
00:14:29,940 --> 00:14:32,797
I actually thought you'd
plunge to your own death.

240
00:14:32,880 --> 00:14:34,645
You scared the crap out of me.

241
00:14:35,020 --> 00:14:38,373
Was it zippers you used to
cling onto the wall like that?

242
00:14:41,200 --> 00:14:42,612
It must have been close.

243
00:14:42,880 --> 00:14:45,821
Looks like you didn't get
an ounce of mold on you.

244
00:14:47,500 --> 00:14:49,537
Hey, Mista, you should get some rest.

245
00:14:49,620 --> 00:14:52,137
I closed your wounds, but they
could start bleeding again.

246
00:14:52,220 --> 00:14:56,657
You just sit back and let me keep a
lookout for any cars that are on our tail.

247
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:57,570
Yeah.

248
00:15:15,480 --> 00:15:17,177
Bucciarati, your wrist is injured.

249
00:15:17,260 --> 00:15:18,837
It looks pretty bad from here.

250
00:15:18,920 --> 00:15:20,096
Let me patch you up.

251
00:15:23,320 --> 00:15:25,037
Hey, Bucciarati, are you listening?

252
00:15:25,120 --> 00:15:27,477
There's a chance the mold
has infected your wound.

253
00:15:27,560 --> 00:15:28,795
Please let me see it.

254
00:15:33,960 --> 00:15:35,040
What are you...

255
00:15:37,800 --> 00:15:38,957
Wait, what the hell?

256
